=== gmlora F_55230_077b4106_0_medium finish=stop usage={'prompt_tokens': 1238, 'total_tokens': 1856, 'completion_tokens': 618, 'prompt_tokens_details': None, 'completion_tokens_details': {'reasoning_tokens': 168}}
REASONING: ' Start with cylindrical stock sized to the printed 45.3 mm diameter, giving a 22.65 mm radius.\n2. Turn the main body to the printed 45.3 mm diameter for a length of 60 mm.\n3. Turn the reduced end section to the printed 38.4 mm diameter, giving a 19.2 mm radius, for a length of 20 mm.\n4. Face the end of the reduced section to establish the overall length of 80 mm.\n5. Drill a 5 mm diameter hole through the center of the reduced end section.\n6. Counterbore the hole to 8 mm diameter by 4 mm deep from the end face.\n7. Apply a 2 mm fillet to all sharp edges.'
CONTENT: '```python\nfrom build123d import *\n\nbody_length = 60.0\nbody_radius = 22.65\nshoulder_length = 20.0\nshoulder_radius = 19.2\nfillet_radius = 2.0\nhole_diameter = 5.0\ncounterbore_diameter = 8.0\ncounterbore_depth = 4.0\n\nwith BuildPart() as p:\n    with BuildSketch(Plane.XY) as sk:\n        with BuildLine() as bl:\n            l1 = Line((0, 0), (0, body_radius))\n            l2 = Line(l1 @ 1, (body_length, body_radius))\n            l3 = Line(l2 @ 1, (body_length, shoulder_radius))\n            l4 = Line(l3 @ 1, (body_length + shoulder_length, shoulder_radius))\n            l5 = Line(l4 @ 1, (body_length + shoulder_length, 0))\n            l6 = Line(l5 @ 1, (0, 0))\n        make_face()\n    revolve(axis=Axis.X)\n\nsolid_body = p.part\nsolid_body = fillet(solid_body.edges(), fillet_radius)\n\nhole_x = body_length + shoulder_length\nsolid_body = solid_body - Pos(hole_x, 0, 0) * Rot(0, 90, 0) * Cylinder(hole_diameter / 2, 200)\nsolid_body = solid_body - Pos(hole_x - counterbore_depth / 2, 0, 0) * Rot(0, 90, 0) * Cylinder(counterbore_diameter / 2, counterbore_depth)\n\npart = solid_body\npart.name = "revolved_body_with_holes"\nexport_step(part, "output.step")\n```'
=== gmlora F_55373_ddd74d2f_0_medium finish=stop usage={'prompt_tokens': 1238, 'total_tokens': 1917, 'completion_tokens': 679, 'prompt_tokens_details': None, 'completion_tokens_details': {'reasoning_tokens': 220}}
REASONING: ' Start with stock sufficient to form an L-shaped bracket with a vertical leg 80 tall and a horizontal leg 70 long, both legs 12 thick.\n2. Extrude the L-profile to a depth of 70 to create the main bracket body.\n3. Add a reinforcing rib on the inner face of the vertical leg, centered along the leg height, with a width of 6 and a height of 30.\n4. Drill a 5 diameter hole through the horizontal leg, positioned 20 from the inner corner along the leg.\n5. Drill a second 5 diameter hole through the horizontal leg, positioned 50 from the inner corner along the leg.\n6. Drill a 5 diameter hole through the vertical leg, positioned 20 from the inner corner along the leg.\n7. Drill a second 5 diameter hole through the vertical leg, positioned 50 from the inner corner along the leg.\n8. Apply a 2 radius fil'
CONTENT: '```python\nfrom build123d import *\n\nleg_length = 70.0\nleg_height = 80.0\nthickness = 12.0\ndepth = 70.0\ninner_fillet_radius = 2.0\nhole_diameter = 5.0\nhole_offset = 20.0\nrib_width = 6.0\nrib_height = 30.0\n\nwith BuildPart() as p:\n    with BuildSketch(Plane.XZ) as sk:\n        with BuildLine() as bl:\n            Polyline((0, 0), (leg_length, 0), (leg_length, thickness),\n                     (thickness, thickness), (thickness, leg_height),\n                     (0, leg_height), close=True)\n        make_face()\n    extrude(amount=depth)\n\nsolid_body = p.part\n\ninner_edges = [e for e in solid_body.edges().filter_by(Axis.Y)\n               if abs(e.center().X - thickness) < 1e-3 and abs(e.center().Z - thickness) < 1e-3]\nsolid_body = fillet(inner_edges, inner_fillet_radius)\n\nrib = Pos(thickness/2, depth/2, leg_height/2) * Box(rib_width, depth, rib_height)\nsolid_body = solid_body + rib\n\nhole_r = hole_diameter / 2\nhole_h = depth + 10\nfor x, z in [(hole_offset, thickness/2), (leg_length - hole_offset, thickness/2),\n             (thickness/2, hole_offset), (thickness/2, leg_height - hole_offset)]:\n    solid_body = solid_body - Pos(x, depth/2, z) * Cylinder(hole_r, hole_h)\n\npart = solid_body\npart.name = "L_Bracket"\nexport_step(part, "output.step")\n```'
=== gmlora F_55423_a50f82f4_0_medium finish=stop usage={'prompt_tokens': 1238, 'total_tokens': 1942, 'completion_tokens': 704, 'prompt_tokens_details': None, 'completion_tokens_details': {'reasoning_tokens': 358}}
REASONING: ' Start with a rectangular block of stock measuring 65.5 long by 40 wide by 76.4 tall.\n2. Machine the block to the overall dimensions of 65.5 by 40 by 76.4.\n3. Cut a rectangular pocket into the top face, leaving a 5 thick wall on all sides and a 5 thick floor at the bottom.\n4. Drill a through hole of diameter 3.6 (radius 1.8) centered on the top face.\n5. Cut a slot through the side wall, 10 wide and 30 long, positioned 15 from the centerline.\n6. Cut a second slot through the side wall, 10 wide and 30 long, positioned 15 from the centerline on the opposite side.\n7. Cut a third slot through the side wall, 10 wide and 30 long, positioned 15 from the centerline.\n8. Cut a fourth slot through the side wall, 10 wide and 30 long, positioned 15 from the centerline.\n9. Cut a fifth slot through the si'
CONTENT: '```python\nfrom build123d import *\n\nouter_width = 60.0\nouter_height = 80.0\nouter_depth = 40.0\nwall_thickness = 5.0\nslot_width = 10.0\nslot_length = 30.0\nslot_spacing = 15.0\nnum_slots = 4\nhole_diameter = 3.6\nhole_depth = 12.0\n\nbase = Box(outer_width, outer_depth, outer_height)\ninner = Box(outer_width - 2*wall_thickness, outer_depth - 2*wall_thickness, outer_height - 2*wall_thickness)\nresult = base - inner\n\nfor i in range(num_slots):\n    y_pos = (i - (num_slots - 1) / 2) * slot_spacing\n    slot = Pos(outer_width/2 - wall_thickness/2, y_pos, 0) * Box(wall_thickness, slot_width, slot_length)\n    result = result - slot\n\nhole = Pos(-outer_width/2 + wall_thickness + hole_depth/2, 0, 0) * Rot(0, 90, 0) * Cylinder(hole_diameter/2, hole_depth)\nresult = result - hole\n\npart = result\npart.name = "hollow_box_with_slots_and_hole"\nexport_step(part, "output.step")\n```'
